# nr-office-engine-open-create: mode selection, open, create, attach, working copies (mixdog-office::session) and the portable OOXML front (mixdog-ooxml::portable)

Written without cargo: nothing below has been compiled (the lead compiles the wave). The modules are a library the Office tool's
dispatch (a later task of the office track: nr-office-engine-qa-finalize-dispatch) calls; this task registers no protocol method and
no service, so nothing is removed from SERVICE_PENDING in compose_flip.rs.

It needs two wires of earlier tasks applied first, and builds on them: `pub mod snapshot;` in mixdog-office/src/lib.rs
(nr-office-engine-snapshot.wire: the working-copy module re-exports its `read_com_saved_copy`) and `pub mod writer;` in
mixdog-office-pdf/src/lib.rs (nr-office-pdf-writer.wire: create writes a PDF with `mixdog_office_pdf::writer::create_pdf`).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office/src/session/mod.rs
After `pub mod design;` add (alphabetical with the existing `pub mod registry;`):

    pub mod create;
    pub mod mode;
    pub mod open;
    pub mod working_copy;

and extend the crate doc by four bullets after `- [`registry`]: ...`:

    //! - [`mode`]: `selectMode` (which backend and mode holds a document) and the Microsoft Office host open and create go through.
    //! - [`open`]: opening and attaching, legacy conversion, `resolveSession` and the session record both open and create build.
    //! - [`create`]: creating a document (every format, the refusals, overwriting), authored documents, the PDF an author action printed.
    //! - [`working_copy`]: the working-copy paths and `materializeWorkingCopy`.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office/src/session/registry.rs
`materializeWorkingCopy` takes the session out of the document index under the path it held and puts it there under the working copy,
and Node's `Map` keeps the session where it was in the sessions map. The registry has no such step (release also drops the session
from the sessions map; index adds without removing), so `working_copy::materialize_working_copy` calls `Registry::retarget`. In
`impl Registry`, after `release`, add:

    /// `materializeWorkingCopy`'s index step: the document index drops the path the session held (when it still names this session),
    /// the session takes `target`, and the index names it under the new path. The session keeps its place in the sessions map.
    pub fn retarget(&self, env: &Environment, handle: &SessionHandle, target: String) {
        let (id, held) = {
            let session = lock(handle);
            (session.id.clone(), session.target.clone())
        };
        let (old_key, new_key) = (document_session_key(env, &held), document_session_key(env, &target));
        {
            let mut tables = self.tables();
            if tables.documents.get(&old_key) == Some(&id) {
                tables.documents.shift_remove(&old_key);
            }
            tables.documents.insert(new_key, id);
        }
        lock(handle).target = target;
    }

(the tables' lock is not held while the session's is taken, as the rest of the registry keeps it.) Add a test beside the others:
retargeting a session leaves its place in `ids()` and moves its document key; a newer session that holds the old path keeps it.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml/src/lib.rs
After `pub mod xlsx_charts;` add `pub mod portable;` and extend the crate doc by one sentence: `portable` is the front of the engine
(`portable-ooxml.mjs`): `apply_portable_ooxml_batch` over the three dispatchers, and the readers, validators, renderer and converter
named in one place.

