## native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json (the index of the fixture sets)
Add to `sets` (after "office-library" or wherever "office-open-create" sorts):

    { "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-open-create.mjs --tree <tree>", "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-open-create/MANIFEST.json", "manifestSha256": "8f52aa4fa732d64d6aa752bd207d74a5c1475a8e64e5df534b42d8a27d4de3ac",
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-open-create.mjs", "set": "office-open-create", "totalBytes": 344052 }

native/core/fixtures/office-open-create/{golden.json,MANIFEST.json} are written at their paths in the worktree and added with
`git add --sparse` (the fixtures folder is not checked out there). The recording was made from `D:/mixdog-build/mig/ref/node` (the copy
of the product at 0bf8fe045) with `--modules` naming a folder with node_modules, because that copy has none and C:/Project/mixdog is not
readable to an engineer: the manifest's `product` is therefore only `{ tree, treeKind: export }`. The recorder runs LibreOffice hidden and
Microsoft Office scripted (it rewrites two Node modules as they load), so a second recording needs no Office and no LibreOffice. The
golden holds the zip parts of every package and the hex of the fixture documents; those bytes are jszip's, so a re-recording changes
golden.json (the manifest digests with it) without changing what the test compares. Re-record once from the integration checkout
(`node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-open-create.mjs --tree <Node product tree>`) and update the digests above.

## Interfaces the dispatch calls (crate mixdog-office, `mixdog_office::session`)
- `mode::select_mode(&host, requested: Option<&Value>, format, source) -> Result<Selected { mode, backend }, String>` (`selectMode`);
  `mode::requested_mode(Option<&Value>) -> String` (`String(x || 'auto').toLowerCase()`), `mode::validate_author_mode`
  (`validatePptxAuthorMode`). `mode::OfficeHost` is Microsoft Office as open and create see it (`supported`, `detect`, `open_session`);
  `impl OfficeHost for mixdog_office_com::OfficeCom` is in the module. The futures are not required to be Send.
- `open::SessionEnv { design: &Context<L> (the design library's lane, environment, fetch and indexer), note: &dyn WriteNote, registry,
  host: &H, legacy: &dyn LegacyConverter, data_dir, cwd, cancel }` is what open, create and attach run with; `cwd` is the call's folder
  ("" for none). `open::SofficeConverter { soffice, proof, cancel: Option<&AtomicBool> }` is the production `LegacyConverter`
  (`Soffice::convert_legacy_office`); `LegacyConverter` is a trait so a replay can answer the recorded refusal without LibreOffice.
- `open::open_session(&env, args, read_only) -> Result<OpenedSession { handle, reused }, String>` (`openSession`; `attach` is the same call
  with `mode: "attach"` in `args`), `open::resolve_session(&env, args, read_only) -> Result<ResolvedSession { opened, implicit }, String>`,
  `open::office_open_failure(reason, path)`. `reused` is Node's `session.reused === true`: Node answered a shallow COPY of the registered
  session there; this answers the registered session itself (a copy would let a later `ensure_office_session_design` or `snapshot_version`
  bump be lost), and the dispatch's `if (session.reused) return` becomes `if opened.reused`.
- `create::create_session(&env, &CreateTools { closer, fonts, svg_fonts }, args) -> Result<Created { session, operations }, String>`
  (`createSession`). `operations` is the initial operations after the contract engine renamed the fields a caller drifted on: Node mutated
  `args.operations` in place and the batch that follows read the rewritten form; pass `operations` to it, not `initial_office_operations(args)`.
  `closer: &C where C: open::SessionCloser` is the finalize stage's `closeSession` (the overwrite of a file a session holds closes that
  session first): the qa-finalize task implements it (`close(&handle) -> Result<(), String>`).
  `create::create_authored_session(&env, args, target)` (`createAuthoredSession`), `create::register_html_pdf_session(&env, args, target,
  target_existed, receipt)` (`registerHtmlPdfSession`), `create::release_overwritten_session`, `create::initial_office_operations(args)`.
- `create::remove_failed_create(proof, &created, initial_edit_settled)` is the FILE half of `discardFailedOfficeSession`
  (office-actions-open.mjs): the empty file a create wrote itself and whose initial operations then failed is removed. The other half (closing
  the Microsoft Office session, `Registry::release`) is the dispatch's `open_action.rs`.
- `working_copy::{full_path, default_output, default_render_output, assert_document_output, editable_target, materialize_working_copy}`;
  `working_copy::read_com_saved_copy` is the snapshot module's (`readComSavedCopy` lives there: the snapshot of a protected sheet needs it).
- `mixdog_ooxml::portable::apply_portable_ooxml_batch(proof, note, measurer, path, format, operations) -> Result<Vec<Value>, String>`
  (`applyPortableOoxmlBatch`: load, the format's dispatcher, the orphan-part sweep after delete_slide/replace_image/delete_shape, the
  table-of-contents refresh of a Word document, save); the module also re-exports the fronts of portable-ooxml.mjs that live in the format
  modules (`snapshot_portable_ooxml`, `validate_portable_ooxml`, `issues_portable_ooxml`, `remove_orphan_package_parts`,
  `inspect_pptx_text_boxes`, `clear_portable_presentation_slides`, `image_pixel_size`, `replace_across_runs`, `recalculate_*`, `Soffice`,
  `RenderFormat`, `create_portable_ooxml_document`).

## What was not compiled
Nothing was compiled or run in Rust. The twin test `tests/twin_open_create.rs` is `#![cfg(windows)]` (the recording is of Windows paths) and
replays at once (`every_answer_equals_the_recording`); the first compile of the four session modules and `portable.rs` is the lead's.
